Package: llutils
Title: Multithreaded Matching and Regex Detection for Large Vectors
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Lukas", "Jung", , "jung-lukas@gmx.net", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Multithreaded versions of match(), %in%, and grepl(),
    written in Rust. match() and %in% give the same results as base R, and
    fall back to it below the size where threads pay off. Regex detection
    uses the syntax of Rust's regex crate. Dictionary lookup finds which of
    many literal terms each string contains, in one pass per string.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
Depends: 
    R (>= 4.3)
Suggests: 
    ggbeeswarm,
    ggplot2,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    withr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/rextendr/version: 0.5.0
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc >= 1.83.0, xz
URL: https://github.com/lhdjung/llutils
BugReports: https://github.com/lhdjung/llutils/issues
